---
import { ANALYTICS_MIN_QUERY_SEARCHES, analyticsKeepDays, PLAN_IDS, PLANS } from "@emojisense/platform";
import Callout from "../../components/docs/Callout.astro";
import DocsLayout from "../../components/docs/DocsLayout.astro";
import { formatDays } from "../../lib/format";

const keep = PLAN_IDS.map((id) => `${PLANS[id].name} ${formatDays(analyticsKeepDays(PLANS[id]))}`).join(", ");
---

<DocsLayout path="/docs/privacy/">
  <h2 id="short-version">The short version</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Most searches never leave the device.</li>
    <li>Emojisense never logs or stores IP addresses, keys or user identifiers.</li>
    <li>Message text for reaction suggestions and images for photo to emoji are never stored.</li>
    <li>Query text is normalized and cut to 64 characters. A query is named in analytics, or used by Emojisense’s own jobs, only after it was seen at least {ANALYTICS_MIN_QUERY_SEARCHES} times.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2 id="where-searches-go">Where each request goes</h2>
  <div class="table-scroll" tabindex="0">
    <table>
      <thead>
        <tr>
          <th scope="col">Layer</th>
          <th scope="col">What leaves the device</th>
          <th scope="col">What is kept</th>
        </tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td>On-device dictionary</td><td>Nothing</td><td>Nothing</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Precomputed results (shards)</td><td>A request for one static file, named by the first letters of the query</td><td>Nothing. Static files are not logged or metered.</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Worker search</td><td>The query, normalized and cut to 64 characters</td><td>The normalized query with cache status and latency, without app, key or IP. For keyed calls, also daily counts per app (see below).</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Reaction suggestions</td><td>The message text, cut to 256 characters</td><td>Nothing. The text is never logged or cached.</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Photo to emoji</td><td>A small, downscaled image</td><td>With an image hash, a short caption cached by that hash. The image itself is dropped after use.</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>

  <h2 id="what-is-kept">What is kept, and for how long</h2>
  <div class="table-scroll" tabindex="0">
    <table>
      <thead><tr><th scope="col">Data</th><th scope="col">Where</th><th scope="col">Kept</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td>Per app, UTC day and normalized query: the number of searches and of misses. Keyed <code>/v1/search</code> calls only.</td><td>D1 <code>query_daily</code></td><td>By plan: {keep}. A daily job deletes older rows.</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Normalized query text of every search that reached the Worker, with cache status, latency and scores. No app.</td><td>Cloudflare Analytics Engine</td><td>The Analytics Engine retention (3 months)</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Monthly call counts per app and metric</td><td>D1 <code>usage_monthly</code></td><td>While the app exists</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>
  <p>Anonymous calls and development keys never reach the per-app table. The dashboard shows analytics only on plans that include them. The source of truth is the privacy section of the <a href="/docs/api/#privacy">HTTP API reference</a>.</p>

  <h2 id="how-queries-are-used">How Emojisense uses queries</h2>
  <p>A nightly job reads only the queries that were seen at least {ANALYTICS_MIN_QUERY_SEARCHES} times. Rare strings can be personal, so they are never used. The frequent queries become precomputed results and new aliases, which make search better for every app.</p>

  <h2 id="rate-limits">Rate limits without tracking</h2>
  <p>Rate limits need to tell callers apart. The Worker uses the IP address only as an in-memory key for the limiter. It is never written to logs or storage.</p>

  <h2 id="this-website">This website</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>No cookies, no analytics and no third-party scripts. Fonts are served from this site.</li>
    <li>The live demos use the Emojisense API like any app. They load the data packs and send unsure searches. They send message text or a photo only when you try those demos, under the rules above.</li>
    <li>The waitlist form sends your email and the plan you chose to the dashboard. The address is used only to tell you when the plan opens.</li>
  </ul>

  <Callout type="privacy" title="Questions">
    <p>The API Worker is open source (MIT). Read <code>packages/worker</code> to see exactly what it records.</p>
  </Callout>
</DocsLayout>
